WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.119 --> 00:00:04.474
- What's up, Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:04.474 --> 00:00:06.526
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:08.859
that you have something special to offer

00:00:08.859 --> 00:00:10.945
and I'd love to see it explode,

00:00:10.945 --> 00:00:13.014
so that you can help change the planet.

00:00:13.014 --> 00:00:14.174
So, to help you on your journey today,

00:00:14.174 --> 00:00:16.804
we're going to look at the
seven types of investors

00:00:16.804 --> 00:00:19.664
for your business and how to find them.

00:00:19.664 --> 00:00:21.747
- [Narrator] Nine, eight.

00:00:22.684 --> 00:00:25.936
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:25.936 --> 00:00:27.274
Seven.

00:00:27.274 --> 00:00:28.906
- So, one of the most
common questions I get asked

00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:30.835
from entrepreneurs is,
how do I fund my business?

00:00:30.835 --> 00:00:31.926
Where do I get investors from?

00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:34.205
I have big dreams, I
want to grow super quick

00:00:34.205 --> 00:00:35.651
and I need money to do it.

00:00:35.651 --> 00:00:37.254
How do I find the people to help me?

00:00:37.254 --> 00:00:38.566
What are they looking for?

00:00:38.566 --> 00:00:40.177
What's the process? Let me know.

00:00:40.177 --> 00:00:42.631
So, today I'm going to you
the seven different kinds

00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:45.507
of investors, and how to
find them for your business.

00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:49.100
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.240
Number one is banks.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.143
Banks are the ones that people seem

00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:52.825
to think about right away.

00:00:52.825 --> 00:00:55.149
People think I need to go
and get money from a bank.

00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:55.982
I need to get a loan.

00:00:55.982 --> 00:00:57.608
I need to apply to get the money in

00:00:57.608 --> 00:00:59.362
to help me grow my business.

00:00:59.362 --> 00:01:03.043
Banks are the least friendly
towards startup entrepreneurs

00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:06.055
of almost all the investment classes.

00:01:06.055 --> 00:01:08.176
Banks don't want to help entrepreneurs.

00:01:08.176 --> 00:01:10.214
Understand what the
business of the bank is in.

00:01:10.214 --> 00:01:13.668
They want to give money to people
who are going to pay them back.

00:01:13.668 --> 00:01:16.040
And startups have the highest failure rate

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.130
of any kind of business, right?

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.755
If you're looking at different classes,

00:01:19.755 --> 00:01:21.299
so why do I want to
give money to a startup?

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:23.512
I don't, banks don't
want to give money to,

00:01:23.512 --> 00:01:25.078
it's not what they have in their marketing

00:01:25.078 --> 00:01:25.911
and their promotions,

00:01:25.911 --> 00:01:28.054
but banks don't want to
give money to startups.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:32.111
Most banks, if you don't
have at least three years

00:01:32.111 --> 00:01:34.762
of history, of financials, and of growth,

00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:36.548
and of making money, then you need

00:01:36.548 --> 00:01:38.858
to personally guarantee the loan.

00:01:38.858 --> 00:01:40.679
And so, then it's really just depending

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:41.803
on your credit history.

00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:43.828
If you have good credit
history, you can get a loan.

00:01:43.828 --> 00:01:46.069
If you don't have good
credit history, you can't.

00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:49.245
But really, you have to wait
until you two, usually three,

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:52.957
years of traction with a
business that's growing

00:01:52.957 --> 00:01:56.285
and making money before
they'll ever give you a loan.

00:01:56.285 --> 00:01:57.247
And so, a lot of people think,

00:01:57.247 --> 00:02:00.365
"Well, I need the money to get there.

00:02:00.365 --> 00:02:02.210
"Once I get there, I don't
need your money anymore,"

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.490
and that's always the
catch 22, where usually you

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.215
get rejected because your
business just hasn't been

00:02:07.215 --> 00:02:09.654
around long enough, unless
you have good personal credit.

00:02:09.654 --> 00:02:11.971
So, banks are definitely
an option, but it's usually

00:02:11.971 --> 00:02:14.067
not the best option for entrepreneurs.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.531
(upbeat pop music)

00:02:17.531 --> 00:02:19.314
Number two is friends and family.

00:02:19.314 --> 00:02:21.330
It's also called blood money.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.904
Here, we're looking at
up to around $50,000.

00:02:23.904 --> 00:02:27.310
So, if you need from $10 to $50,000

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.095
and you're looking for an investor,

00:02:29.095 --> 00:02:31.120
it's usually going to come from friends,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.057
family, kindergarten classmates, you know,

00:02:34.057 --> 00:02:37.273
a friend of a friend,
then an uncle, an aunt,

00:02:37.273 --> 00:02:38.358
you know, something like that.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.093
It usually not your most
immediate connections,

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:43.041
but it's one or two or three degrees away,

00:02:43.041 --> 00:02:45.483
a friend of a friend of
a friend kind of thing.

00:02:45.483 --> 00:02:48.829
And if it's $50,000 or less that you need,

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:50.986
it's usually an unsophisticated investor.

00:02:50.986 --> 00:02:52.710
It's not a big-time investor because

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:53.946
it's just not worth it to them.

00:02:53.946 --> 00:02:56.117
The amount of work to
understand your business

00:02:56.117 --> 00:02:57.654
to help mentor and train you,

00:02:57.654 --> 00:02:58.960
it's just not worth it to them.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.551
And so, that's where you usually deal

00:03:00.551 --> 00:03:02.539
with more unsophisticated people.

00:03:02.539 --> 00:03:04.384
Usually, they look for like they know you,

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.005
they like you, they trust you.

00:03:06.005 --> 00:03:07.661
They want to see you be successful.

00:03:07.661 --> 00:03:09.484
Here you can play the guilt card.

00:03:09.484 --> 00:03:13.254
Remember when I helped you move that piano

00:03:13.254 --> 00:03:15.393
to that other apartment that you had.

00:03:15.393 --> 00:03:16.933
And I've been here for you, right?

00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:19.161
Like you're playin' on heartstrings,

00:03:19.161 --> 00:03:21.005
which investors, like
sophisticated investors

00:03:21.005 --> 00:03:22.429
won't care as much about,

00:03:22.429 --> 00:03:24.711
but friends and family
will care more about.

00:03:24.711 --> 00:03:26.868
And basically, they want to see a return,

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:29.031
but it's more that they
like you, they know you,

00:03:29.031 --> 00:03:30.712
they want to see you
succeed, they want to try

00:03:30.712 --> 00:03:32.618
to help out in every way they can.

00:03:32.618 --> 00:03:34.232
The thing to be careful about is,

00:03:34.232 --> 00:03:36.448
do you want them to be a
part of your company or not?

00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:39.904
Like, do you want Aunt Jill
to be in your business?

00:03:39.904 --> 00:03:41.416
Do you want her helping manage it?

00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:43.479
Do you want to be taking her advice?

00:03:43.479 --> 00:03:45.014
Are they just giving you money,

00:03:45.014 --> 00:03:46.779
or are they going to play an active role?

00:03:46.779 --> 00:03:48.512
Is it going to be a problem
when you get together

00:03:48.512 --> 00:03:50.831
at Thanksgiving and Aunt Jill is there?

00:03:50.831 --> 00:03:52.676
Just those kinds of things to figure out.

00:03:52.676 --> 00:03:54.087
If it doesn't work out, what happens

00:03:54.087 --> 00:03:55.456
with your relationship with Aunt Jill

00:03:55.456 --> 00:03:57.411
and the family and all that stuff?

00:03:57.411 --> 00:04:00.311
It can go sideways, so you
really have to be careful

00:04:00.311 --> 00:04:02.786
about working with friends and family,

00:04:02.786 --> 00:04:04.346
but it could also work
out in a positive sense.

00:04:04.346 --> 00:04:06.363
But if it's under $50,000,
you're really looking

00:04:06.363 --> 00:04:08.296
at friends and family, relatives,

00:04:08.296 --> 00:04:10.685
friend of friends, to get that funded.

00:04:10.685 --> 00:04:14.051
(upbeat pop music)

00:04:14.051 --> 00:04:15.679
Way number three are angels.

00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:17.375
Angels are angel investors.

00:04:17.375 --> 00:04:19.435
They are usually successful individuals

00:04:19.435 --> 00:04:21.548
who built a business for themselves,

00:04:21.548 --> 00:04:24.232
they're entrepreneurs, or they're
a successful professional,

00:04:24.232 --> 00:04:25.973
and they're looking to invest money

00:04:25.973 --> 00:04:28.923
into a company to make some more money.

00:04:28.923 --> 00:04:31.400
A lot of times, there's a category gap

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.627
between the entrepreneurs, the people

00:04:33.627 --> 00:04:34.891
who are sophisticated investors,

00:04:34.891 --> 00:04:37.121
the people who used to taking companies

00:04:37.121 --> 00:04:38.652
and ramping them up quickly

00:04:38.652 --> 00:04:40.939
versus just people who have money.

00:04:40.939 --> 00:04:42.791
And there's a term in
the industry called DDI,

00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:45.292
which is dentists and doctors
with disposable income.

00:04:45.292 --> 00:04:47.394
A lot of times, these
guys have a lot of money,

00:04:47.394 --> 00:04:49.034
'cause they're a dentist
and they make a lot of money

00:04:49.034 --> 00:04:53.211
in their practice, and they,
as my dentist explained,

00:04:53.211 --> 00:04:54.539
are kind of bored in their life,

00:04:54.539 --> 00:04:57.572
and they like to live through
their investments, right?

00:04:57.572 --> 00:04:59.393
So, they're buying
stocks, and real estate,

00:04:59.393 --> 00:05:01.298
and all this other stuff,
and then take a portion

00:05:01.298 --> 00:05:02.566
to invest in the startups, because they

00:05:02.566 --> 00:05:03.750
want a little of excitement.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.632
They want to be able to
brag to their friends,

00:05:05.632 --> 00:05:08.365
and they want to see
something exciting happening,

00:05:08.365 --> 00:05:09.561
because their own business is kind

00:05:09.561 --> 00:05:11.690
of boring and traditional.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:15.011
And so, that's a dangerous
kind of investor to look for.

00:05:15.011 --> 00:05:17.537
Anytime you're bringing
somebody on at that level,

00:05:17.537 --> 00:05:19.886
you ideally want somebody
who can help you,

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:23.478
who can bring value to
you, give you connections,

00:05:23.478 --> 00:05:26.141
open up doors to you,
not just give you money.

00:05:26.141 --> 00:05:28.512
So, it's dumb money, you
don't want dumb money.

00:05:28.512 --> 00:05:29.512
You want smart money.

00:05:29.512 --> 00:05:31.108
You want people who care,
who've done this before.

00:05:31.108 --> 00:05:32.865
It's not their first rodeo, and they can

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.878
open up doors and connections for you.

00:05:34.878 --> 00:05:35.922
And so, it's really important.

00:05:35.922 --> 00:05:39.062
At the start it can be hard
because you need the money.

00:05:39.062 --> 00:05:40.443
You need the money to grow in scale

00:05:40.443 --> 00:05:43.068
and build this thing up,
and you don't want to wait,

00:05:43.068 --> 00:05:45.849
but if you have a bad angel investor,

00:05:45.849 --> 00:05:47.228
it's hard to get rid of them.

00:05:47.228 --> 00:05:50.243
And it can hurt your
future potential rounds.

00:05:50.243 --> 00:05:52.772
If you ever want to go get
venture capital in the next step,

00:05:52.772 --> 00:05:54.655
they look at who your angel investors are.

00:05:54.655 --> 00:05:57.004
And if it's a bunch of
people with no experience

00:05:57.004 --> 00:05:58.522
and they're just giving you money,

00:05:58.522 --> 00:05:59.984
it's really hard to get the next round.

00:05:59.984 --> 00:06:01.610
So, you really want to be careful

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.440
who you're getting the money from.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.668
A great way to start is
just through connections,

00:06:05.668 --> 00:06:09.164
lawyers, accountants, bookkeepers,
those kinds of people.

00:06:09.164 --> 00:06:11.830
Talk to your lawyer, talk to
any lawyer that you can kind

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.881
of make a connection with
through friends, family,

00:06:13.881 --> 00:06:16.682
ask them who their lawyers
are, who their accountants are.

00:06:16.682 --> 00:06:20.554
'Cause those guys also do
legal work and accounting work

00:06:20.554 --> 00:06:23.199
for bigger players, for angel investors.

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:26.210
Most angels are not, they
don't have a website.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.731
They don't say I'm an angel investor

00:06:27.731 --> 00:06:30.141
because then they get pitched constantly.

00:06:30.141 --> 00:06:31.892
A lot of the angel investment deals happen

00:06:31.892 --> 00:06:33.653
through word of mouth and networking.

00:06:33.653 --> 00:06:35.475
And so, talking to lawyers and accountants

00:06:35.475 --> 00:06:37.150
are a great way to be able to do that.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.465
So, I try to make a list
of 30 different lawyers

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.345
that I can go and meet,

00:06:40.345 --> 00:06:42.387
and three different
accountants I can go and meet,

00:06:42.387 --> 00:06:44.532
through introductions
through friends and family.

00:06:44.532 --> 00:06:46.046
And tell them what your idea is,

00:06:46.046 --> 00:06:48.379
and that'll turn the radar
and they're thinking about it.

00:06:48.379 --> 00:06:50.046
For angel investors in
general, they want to see

00:06:50.046 --> 00:06:51.586
that they're making a return, right?

00:06:51.586 --> 00:06:53.937
They want to be able to get
out in six to eight years,

00:06:53.937 --> 00:06:56.099
so there's a path to exit
and get their money back.

00:06:56.099 --> 00:07:00.018
And they want to be making
around 25 to 30% per year.

00:07:00.018 --> 00:07:01.138
That's what's going to
happen at the beginning.

00:07:01.138 --> 00:07:02.901
You're probably going to
lose money at the beginning,

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:04.604
but net, like when you end up selling,

00:07:04.604 --> 00:07:08.357
they've made a 25 to 30%
annual return on their deal.

00:07:08.357 --> 00:07:10.338
So, that's not possible
in every industry, right?

00:07:10.338 --> 00:07:12.919
Like if you're in a slow-paced industry,

00:07:12.919 --> 00:07:14.908
if you're in a retail store,
that's going to be hard

00:07:14.908 --> 00:07:16.623
to get those kinds of returns.

00:07:16.623 --> 00:07:18.216
So, it may not be a good fit for you

00:07:18.216 --> 00:07:20.161
to be going after angel investors,

00:07:20.161 --> 00:07:21.960
but in general, that's what they look for.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.925
And the range is between
50,000 and 250,000.

00:07:25.925 --> 00:07:28.037
On the 50,000, again, you're
looking at friends and family.

00:07:28.037 --> 00:07:30.359
Over 250,000 you're looking at more

00:07:30.359 --> 00:07:32.209
of an institutional
investor, who are looking

00:07:32.209 --> 00:07:33.928
at venture capital and other kinds.

00:07:33.928 --> 00:07:35.832
It's hard for a single person

00:07:35.832 --> 00:07:37.873
to write a million dollar check.

00:07:37.873 --> 00:07:41.656
It's possible, but most angels
play in a smaller arena.

00:07:41.656 --> 00:07:43.661
And so, that's kind of the
range that you're looking for

00:07:43.661 --> 00:07:44.929
and how to get introduced to them.

00:07:44.929 --> 00:07:48.423
(upbeat pop music)

00:07:48.423 --> 00:07:50.268
All right, way number
four is venture capital.

00:07:50.268 --> 00:07:51.177
This is the big daddy.

00:07:51.177 --> 00:07:52.957
This is the people with tons of money.

00:07:52.957 --> 00:07:55.174
They raise funds of hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:57.753
and try to invest it into
high-growth companies

00:07:57.753 --> 00:08:00.015
to see major returns.

00:08:00.015 --> 00:08:03.199
Angels start in the 250 range,

00:08:03.199 --> 00:08:04.723
they don't really want to be there.

00:08:04.723 --> 00:08:06.615
They want to be in the millions range,

00:08:06.615 --> 00:08:09.301
because again, the amount
of work that's required

00:08:09.301 --> 00:08:11.913
in doing a deal is pretty much the same.

00:08:11.913 --> 00:08:14.881
If a VC's putting $5
million into a company,

00:08:14.881 --> 00:08:16.096
the amount of work to research

00:08:16.096 --> 00:08:18.256
and do the due diligence
is pretty much the same,

00:08:18.256 --> 00:08:22.935
if not less, than doin' the
work on a $250,000 deal.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.758
Because by the time you've hit that mark,

00:08:24.758 --> 00:08:26.897
you've had some success,
you've had more traction,

00:08:26.897 --> 00:08:28.414
and you're more of a known quantity.

00:08:28.414 --> 00:08:29.610
Where it's a lot of work to invest

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.759
and to understand a newer company.

00:08:31.759 --> 00:08:34.173
And so, they don't really want
to play in that low range,

00:08:34.173 --> 00:08:37.024
but they're hoping that
if they give you 250K,

00:08:37.024 --> 00:08:40.051
then you'll come back for
the next round of a million,

00:08:40.051 --> 00:08:42.406
the next round of five
million, and continue to grow.

00:08:42.406 --> 00:08:44.019
Venture capitalists are also looking

00:08:44.019 --> 00:08:47.812
for 30%, 25 to 30% annual return.

00:08:47.812 --> 00:08:49.205
And they want to be out shorter.

00:08:49.205 --> 00:08:51.730
So, they want to be out in
four to five years typically.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.404
They want to see that
there's a path to exit,

00:08:53.404 --> 00:08:56.028
so that you're going to get acquired,
somebody's going to buy you.

00:08:56.028 --> 00:08:58.004
Or you're going to go
IPO, so you're going to go

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.053
to the stock market.

00:08:59.053 --> 00:09:01.236
Not that many companies
make it to the stock market.

00:09:01.236 --> 00:09:04.437
So typically, they want
to look for acquisition.

00:09:04.437 --> 00:09:07.023
So, as part of your plan, you want to show

00:09:07.023 --> 00:09:09.592
who's going to buy you,
that there's an appetite,

00:09:09.592 --> 00:09:12.160
that there's some big company
or multiple big companies

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.025
that will potentially want to buy you up

00:09:14.025 --> 00:09:16.858
as you build and scale your business.

00:09:16.858 --> 00:09:18.923
And so, understanding that is
going to be super important

00:09:18.923 --> 00:09:20.317
whenever you go and make a pitch.

00:09:20.317 --> 00:09:21.391
And again, venture capitalists,

00:09:21.391 --> 00:09:22.784
now these guys do have websites.

00:09:22.784 --> 00:09:25.132
You can cold pitch, you can cold email.

00:09:25.132 --> 00:09:26.518
I was on the other side of that.

00:09:26.518 --> 00:09:28.391
I was receiving the cold pitches

00:09:28.391 --> 00:09:30.015
and emails from entrepreneurs.

00:09:30.015 --> 00:09:34.178
99% of people get rejected,
so your better path in

00:09:34.178 --> 00:09:35.588
is again, through a connection,

00:09:35.588 --> 00:09:37.770
through a lawyer, through an accountant.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.779
Again, those are great
potential paths for you.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:41.719
Through your angel investor
that you made a smart decision

00:09:41.719 --> 00:09:44.623
with to get the right
one to help bump you up.

00:09:44.623 --> 00:09:46.861
And again, remember, for any investor,

00:09:46.861 --> 00:09:48.389
they want to look at use of proceeds.

00:09:48.389 --> 00:09:49.826
That's how you're going
to be spending the money.

00:09:49.826 --> 00:09:52.670
They want to see that you're
spending it on smart things.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:53.943
So, you're paying yourself a salary,

00:09:53.943 --> 00:09:56.629
but it's not an insane salary, right?

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:58.127
Like you're not paying yourself a 100K

00:09:58.127 --> 00:09:59.467
to start this business.

00:09:59.467 --> 00:10:01.997
They want to see that everything's
going into the company.

00:10:01.997 --> 00:10:03.987
They're not interested in
paying you a huge salary.

00:10:03.987 --> 00:10:06.367
They're not interested in
buying out another investor.

00:10:06.367 --> 00:10:10.688
Or a lot of times where somebody
would come to us and say,

00:10:10.688 --> 00:10:13.852
"We want to raise money, we
need a half a million dollars,

00:10:13.852 --> 00:10:14.773
"and half of it's going to be used

00:10:14.773 --> 00:10:16.751
"to buy out our first angel investor."

00:10:16.751 --> 00:10:17.953
Not interested.

00:10:17.953 --> 00:10:19.433
They don't want to buy
out another investor.

00:10:19.433 --> 00:10:21.672
They want to see the money's
being used to grow the business,

00:10:21.672 --> 00:10:24.336
and that your big payday's
not coming from your salary,

00:10:24.336 --> 00:10:25.939
it's going to be when
you build this company

00:10:25.939 --> 00:10:27.373
and eventually sell it.

00:10:27.373 --> 00:10:28.819
Your investment is in the shares

00:10:28.819 --> 00:10:31.261
of owning that business
and then being acquired,

00:10:31.261 --> 00:10:33.072
much more than how much
you're going to get paid.

00:10:33.072 --> 00:10:34.176
So, you want to make sure you're keeping

00:10:34.176 --> 00:10:37.190
your salary expectations really in check,

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.869
getting paid like less
than industry standard,

00:10:39.869 --> 00:10:41.630
because your heart and soul, blood, sweat,

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.562
and tears are going into
building this business.

00:10:43.562 --> 00:10:46.970
(upbeat pop music)

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:48.671
Way number five is through customers.

00:10:48.671 --> 00:10:50.424
And this is a great path to do it,

00:10:50.424 --> 00:10:53.015
where you're not giving up
any equity in your business.

00:10:53.015 --> 00:10:55.488
And this is where you are
pre-selling your products,

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:57.567
your services before you even launch it.

00:10:57.567 --> 00:10:59.863
And so, this is where
Kickstarter comes in,

00:10:59.863 --> 00:11:01.125
and all of those kinds of companies

00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:02.946
where you are marketing a product,

00:11:02.946 --> 00:11:05.110
maybe you build a prototype,
you make a video of it,

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:06.563
you show off what it can do,

00:11:06.563 --> 00:11:09.459
and before ever going into production,

00:11:09.459 --> 00:11:11.180
you're getting orders and sales.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.870
This is a fantastic way to do it,

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.889
because it allows you to test something.

00:11:14.889 --> 00:11:17.791
Before ordering 10,000 of whatever product

00:11:17.791 --> 00:11:21.345
you're going to make, you make
one, you show that it works,

00:11:21.345 --> 00:11:23.726
and then you create a campaign
to market and promote it.

00:11:23.726 --> 00:11:25.779
And if it takes off,
then you have the funds

00:11:25.779 --> 00:11:27.086
to be able to go out and do it.

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:29.113
You don't need to go out and
raise capital from anybody.

00:11:29.113 --> 00:11:30.859
And you don't lose a
chunk of your company.

00:11:30.859 --> 00:11:32.458
And you're not saddled with a ton of debt.

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:35.574
And if it doesn't work out,
then you don't make the product,

00:11:35.574 --> 00:11:37.444
and all you're out is that one prototype,

00:11:37.444 --> 00:11:39.563
which cost you some
money and probably tons

00:11:39.563 --> 00:11:41.243
of time and effort and labor,

00:11:41.243 --> 00:11:44.724
but it wasn't this huge gigantic expense.

00:11:44.724 --> 00:11:47.322
And so, if you can do
it, it's a fantastic way

00:11:47.322 --> 00:11:49.093
to get the funding for your business.

00:11:49.093 --> 00:11:52.199
And also, less of a dog and pony show,

00:11:52.199 --> 00:11:54.317
where typically like to raise
money from venture capital,

00:11:54.317 --> 00:11:58.390
VCs, angels, even friends and
family can take a lot of time.

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:02.310
And it takes away from you
actually building your business.

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:04.551
It's almost a full time job
pitching to venture capitalists,

00:12:04.551 --> 00:12:07.571
which is time you're not spending
on building your company.

00:12:07.571 --> 00:12:09.602
And so, if you can get those pre-orders,

00:12:09.602 --> 00:12:12.294
especially at the beginning,
and show that there's interest.

00:12:12.294 --> 00:12:14.867
Like, if you have interest,
and you have sales coming in,

00:12:14.867 --> 00:12:18.761
it's way easier to then
get expansion capital

00:12:18.761 --> 00:12:21.541
from friends and family, from angels,

00:12:21.541 --> 00:12:23.198
from venture capitalists
to really build it

00:12:23.198 --> 00:12:25.024
to the next step up.

00:12:25.024 --> 00:12:27.673
But I definitely encourage you
to explore getting customers

00:12:27.673 --> 00:12:30.711
to fund it, because you're
not risking anything

00:12:30.711 --> 00:12:32.514
besides a little bit of time,

00:12:32.514 --> 00:12:34.580
and you're not giving up a
huge chunk of your company.

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:38.071
(upbeat pop music)

00:12:38.071 --> 00:12:39.383
Way number six is through the government.

00:12:39.383 --> 00:12:41.471
Governments, depending on where you live,

00:12:41.471 --> 00:12:43.032
will have various different programs.

00:12:43.032 --> 00:12:45.496
They have it at a city level,
at a state or province level,

00:12:45.496 --> 00:12:48.125
and at a national level,
lots of different programs

00:12:48.125 --> 00:12:49.765
where you can either get a grant,

00:12:49.765 --> 00:12:50.979
which means they're giving you money

00:12:50.979 --> 00:12:52.243
and you don't have to pay it back.

00:12:52.243 --> 00:12:54.291
Or they give you a loan where
they're giving you money,

00:12:54.291 --> 00:12:56.497
but you have to pay it back with interest

00:12:56.497 --> 00:12:58.070
and at various rates.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.088
A lot of times, government programs are

00:13:00.088 --> 00:13:02.428
for specific kinds of entrepreneurs.

00:13:02.428 --> 00:13:04.870
So, if you are an immigrant
entrepreneur, you can qualify.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:06.627
If you're a woman
entrepreneur, you can qualify.

00:13:06.627 --> 00:13:08.508
If you're a young
entrepreneur, you can qualify.

00:13:08.508 --> 00:13:10.266
If you're a tech
entrepreneur, you can qualify.

00:13:10.266 --> 00:13:13.324
And so, more than anything else,
the government really cares

00:13:13.324 --> 00:13:15.856
about the background of where you're from,

00:13:15.856 --> 00:13:19.424
where for most other
investors, angels, VCs,

00:13:19.424 --> 00:13:21.608
friends and family, they
don't care if you're a woman

00:13:21.608 --> 00:13:24.466
or a man, or Hispanic or.

00:13:24.466 --> 00:13:25.797
They don't care, they
don't care about that.

00:13:25.797 --> 00:13:27.610
They care, is this a good idea?

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.443
Do I believe in this?

00:13:28.443 --> 00:13:29.418
Is this going to make money?

00:13:29.418 --> 00:13:31.064
Does this have a lot of opportunity?

00:13:31.064 --> 00:13:32.749
With the governments,
they care a lot more.

00:13:32.749 --> 00:13:34.605
They have lots of funds
designed specifically

00:13:34.605 --> 00:13:35.836
for different purposes.

00:13:35.836 --> 00:13:38.783
And so, you have to figure
out kind of where you fit it.

00:13:38.783 --> 00:13:40.615
The thing with government
that is really frustrating

00:13:40.615 --> 00:13:42.397
is that it takes a long time.

00:13:42.397 --> 00:13:44.779
And so, it's a lot of work
to find the right program.

00:13:44.779 --> 00:13:47.833
The funds typically aren't huge,

00:13:47.833 --> 00:13:50.231
but I guess every little bit can help.

00:13:50.231 --> 00:13:52.338
It's just you may have
to wait months and months

00:13:52.338 --> 00:13:56.618
and months to first get
approval just to get a yes.

00:13:56.618 --> 00:13:58.617
You may not even get a
yes, 'cause you apply

00:13:58.617 --> 00:14:01.537
and lots of people are applying,
and it's a competition.

00:14:01.537 --> 00:14:04.590
And then even once you get a yes,

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.733
you have to wait for
that money to come in.

00:14:06.733 --> 00:14:08.745
And by that time, your
company may be dead, right?

00:14:08.745 --> 00:14:10.472
Like we need the money now.

00:14:10.472 --> 00:14:13.142
Entrepreneurs are, you know,
we don't have patience.

00:14:13.142 --> 00:14:15.170
We want it to go, let's
go, we're driving forward.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.922
I don't want to wait months for anything.

00:14:16.922 --> 00:14:19.986
And so, that's the biggest
drawback to do with governments.

00:14:19.986 --> 00:14:22.105
The chance of you getting it,

00:14:22.105 --> 00:14:25.266
then being able to wait
for them to give you a yes,

00:14:25.266 --> 00:14:26.766
and all the paperwork, and then being

00:14:26.766 --> 00:14:28.710
with actually get the money.

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:32.855
One other thing is just making
sure to, in the program,

00:14:32.855 --> 00:14:35.903
the how you use the money is also specific

00:14:35.903 --> 00:14:37.622
to a lot of different government programs.

00:14:37.622 --> 00:14:39.371
So, like it can only
be used to buy product.

00:14:39.371 --> 00:14:41.105
It can only be used for R and D.

00:14:41.105 --> 00:14:43.001
It can only be used to hire people.

00:14:43.001 --> 00:14:45.516
Sometimes the use case is super specific.

00:14:45.516 --> 00:14:48.312
And then also, sometimes
the programs prevent you

00:14:48.312 --> 00:14:50.481
from doing something that may

00:14:50.481 --> 00:14:52.166
be outside the interests
of the government.

00:14:52.166 --> 00:14:55.241
So, in Canada, we have programs
that you can get funding

00:14:55.241 --> 00:14:56.897
for your research and development,

00:14:56.897 --> 00:14:58.713
but it has to stay in Canada.

00:14:58.713 --> 00:15:02.872
So, you can't sell your
company to a US based company

00:15:02.872 --> 00:15:05.764
four or five years after
you've gotten that money,

00:15:05.764 --> 00:15:06.979
which could really hurt you.

00:15:06.979 --> 00:15:08.595
Like maybe your goal is
to sell in three years,

00:15:08.595 --> 00:15:10.878
and I can't sell because I made this deal

00:15:10.878 --> 00:15:12.854
with the government, it could be an issue.

00:15:12.854 --> 00:15:14.310
Or it might be within your state.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:16.153
Like everything has to
stay within the state,

00:15:16.153 --> 00:15:18.022
which could hand-tie you from being able

00:15:18.022 --> 00:15:19.842
to sell your company or expand elsewhere.

00:15:19.842 --> 00:15:22.191
So, just pay attention
to the fine details,

00:15:22.191 --> 00:15:23.306
'cause there's going to be a lot of them

00:15:23.306 --> 00:15:24.531
when dealing with the government.

00:15:24.531 --> 00:15:27.990
(upbeat pop music)

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.979
And the number seven way
is through suppliers.

00:15:29.979 --> 00:15:32.276
A lot of times, the suppliers
that you have to buy stuff

00:15:32.276 --> 00:15:35.295
from will be potential
investors for your business.

00:15:35.295 --> 00:15:39.322
One, in either giving you
product, giving you supplies,

00:15:39.322 --> 00:15:40.842
like whatever they're selling you.

00:15:40.842 --> 00:15:43.502
If you want tee-shirts
and they make tee-shirts,

00:15:43.502 --> 00:15:46.986
they may give you the tee-shirts

00:15:46.986 --> 00:15:50.558
in good faith or like as
owning a piece of your company.

00:15:50.558 --> 00:15:52.492
And so, that's how it gets started.

00:15:52.492 --> 00:15:55.308
Or just maybe on a discounted basis.

00:15:55.308 --> 00:15:56.674
Like they believe in your plan.

00:15:56.674 --> 00:15:58.509
They're not taking a
piece of your company.

00:15:58.509 --> 00:16:00.420
They see your vision of
where you want to go.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:03.562
They give you the first run
at a really discounted price

00:16:03.562 --> 00:16:05.574
to help you get started,
and then they're hoping

00:16:05.574 --> 00:16:07.939
to buy your future
business as you get going.

00:16:07.939 --> 00:16:09.823
As an entrepreneur at the beginning,

00:16:09.823 --> 00:16:10.656
you don't have a lot of money.

00:16:10.656 --> 00:16:11.633
You don't have a lot of resources.

00:16:11.633 --> 00:16:12.897
So, you have to be really
resourceful, right?

00:16:12.897 --> 00:16:14.042
You've got to be really creative.

00:16:14.042 --> 00:16:16.407
And one of the ways to do that
is through your suppliers.

00:16:16.407 --> 00:16:17.695
So, look at every deal that you're making

00:16:17.695 --> 00:16:20.155
with your suppliers, try to
find the best deal possible.

00:16:20.155 --> 00:16:21.611
Try to get creative.

00:16:21.611 --> 00:16:23.970
It might be you helping
them with their marketing

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.184
or their website, which may be outside

00:16:26.184 --> 00:16:27.980
of the realm of what you're selling.

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:28.945
But because you're doing that,

00:16:28.945 --> 00:16:31.237
they're going to exchange product with you

00:16:31.237 --> 00:16:33.105
to help you get to where you want to go.

00:16:33.105 --> 00:16:34.625
There may be some of that contra stuff

00:16:34.625 --> 00:16:36.208
at the beginning to get started.

00:16:36.208 --> 00:16:38.152
Or looking for any other
way that you might be able

00:16:38.152 --> 00:16:41.677
to get the product for free
or at a discounted price,

00:16:41.677 --> 00:16:43.598
or potentially have them
invest in your business,

00:16:43.598 --> 00:16:45.191
because they can provide a lot more value

00:16:45.191 --> 00:16:48.404
in the long term, to get those products in

00:16:48.404 --> 00:16:50.899
and help you get your business started.

00:16:50.899 --> 00:16:52.249
So, thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:52.249 --> 00:16:55.132
I made this video because
Bhim Singh asked me to.

00:16:55.132 --> 00:16:56.721
Those are my seven tips, my seven ways

00:16:56.721 --> 00:16:59.306
on the different kinds of
investors and how to find them.

00:16:59.306 --> 00:17:01.033
I'd love to know what do you guys think?

00:17:01.033 --> 00:17:03.539
What was the most applicable
or interesting for you?

00:17:03.539 --> 00:17:05.275
What are you going to apply
immediately to your business?

00:17:05.275 --> 00:17:07.391
Did I miss an eight, nine, 10
you want to add to the list?

00:17:07.391 --> 00:17:09.337
Share it down in the comments below.

